\paragraph{Collaboration and support.}
Collaboration on independent mathematical review, quantitative resource analysis and physically grounded implementations is invited. Funding or institutional support for this independent research programme would be welcome.

\paragraph{AI assistance.}
AI tools were used in mathematical development, literature research, drafting, restructuring and internal checking of this revision. Earlier research in the programme also involved substantial GPT-assisted development. This disclosure is not a claim of independent verification, final human validation of every argument, or journal peer review.

\section{Reproduction and revision record}
Run \texttt{python verify\_equilibrium.py} in the source directory using the stated NumPy, SciPy, SymPy and Matplotlib environment. The script writes \texttt{verification\_results.json} and the equation-derived figure. Compile \texttt{equilibrium\_measurement.tex} with pdfLaTeX and BibTeX, or with \texttt{latexmk -pdf}. The accompanying review and source map record the exact earlier-source hash, claim locators, checks performed and outstanding review boundaries.

The principal bounded changes from version 2 are explicit preparation/reference uniformity, the joint symbolic history definition and its constant-hold coupling, literature positioning, and replacement of unverified inherited supplementary-file claims by the supplied reproducible checks. The exact writer, storage, transported reset, internal-gap, massive-clock, archive-current and closure proof structures remain those of the cited predecessor. No source-only numerical bound has been silently transferred from a different Hamiltonian or statistical preparation.
